# Deny everything, then allow back exactly what the build reads. The previous
# denylist shipped whatever appeared next to it: .env (ORIGIN, TRINOCULAR_CONFIG)
# and .claude/worktrees (411 MB of checkouts) were both in the build context,
# and `cache-to: mode=max` exports the builder stage — .env included — to the
# shared GitHub Actions cache. An allowlist fails loudly instead of silently.
*

!bun.lock
!package.json
!svelte.config.ts
!vite.config.ts
!tsconfig.json
!src/
!static/
!packages/

# Re-exclude build state nested inside the allowed trees.
**/node_modules
**/.svelte-kit
**/dist
**/*.timestamp-*
